#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""aitop: one view of every local AI agent session and which ones are waiting on you.

Sources (read-only):
  $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/projects/*/*.jsonl   Claude Code transcripts (CLI, VSCode, Desktop Code tab)
  $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/sessions/<pid>.json  live Claude processes with busy/idle/waiting status
  ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude-code-sessions/   Desktop titles, archive flag, turn summaries (macOS)
  $CODEX_HOME/state_*.sqlite + rollouts   Codex threads from every model provider

aitop writes only its own state: read marks, a usage index and generated briefings (see STATE_DIR, CACHE_DIR).
Briefings send a digest of your sessions to the LLM command in the config file; nothing else leaves the machine.
"""
